## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests a practical CAPA approach for streaming pipelines with region-specific failures.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect, contain, remediate, verify with SLAs
- Minimal REST API for CAPA CRUD with logs/traces and policy links
- Region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA template and canary rollout planning for changes to streaming config

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA type example
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  evidence: { latencyMs?: number; logs?: string[]; watermarkHash?: string; timestamp?: string }[];
  lineage: string[];
  owners: string[];
  region: string;
  status: 'detect'|'contain'|'remediate'|'verify';
  slaMs: number;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate containment under bursty traffic?
- What metrics would you expose to prove recurrence remains zero?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?
